# Purpose
One guide for the shared task list people and agents use for work that
outlives a turn.

# Sanitization
Written fresh from the engine contract and authorization code
(rewrite-only): no service names, routes, ports, stores or error codes.

# Gotchas
- AI and script tasks do NOT start by themselves; keep the bold warning while
  that is true. Update it in the same change that turns runs on.
- The permission table mirrors the engine's single authorization function
  (org: members read, admins manage, assigned member acts; mesh: mesh
  admins manage, assigned mesh member acts; node follows mesh plus node
  owners/admins; private: creator manages, creator and assignee act).
- Schedule limits: lead time 15 min to 7 days (12 h default), catch-up all
  capped at 7, rules DAILY/WEEKLY(BYDAY)/MONTHLY(BYMONTHDAY), interval ≤99.
- Completion record table mirrors the engine outcome rules (summary ≤500
  characters; required for sprint human tasks and ai_then_human approval;
  a person may finish an AI/script task with a summary instead of a card).
- Reminders: due-time reminder for every task; a schedule's notify adds
  remind-before and overdue alerts (agent tool only; the Agenda cannot set
  them). Delivery is an open dashboard only, never phones yet.
- Schedules: people, scripts and AI (kind + instructions); AI occurrences
  still wait for a person to run them. Nodes not updated refuse the new
  fields; the guide says "update from the System card", no release numbers.
- Performer/owner changes are the Agenda's Change assignment; agents cannot.

# Change History
- 2026-11-14: Reminder settings and AI schedules can be created by agents (after the schedule fields fix).
- 2026-11-14: Completion record, reasons, Change assignment, honest reminder and schedule limits, suggestions and reports, link to the agent reference.
- 2026-11-13: Created.

# 2026-11-24 Run authority correction
Supersedes blanket AI-runs-off statements above. Explicit Run now, confirmed Run at due and accepted AI schedules use enabled run services and current permissions; due time alone does not grant execution. Brain mandates cover only admitted kinds and nodes with expiry/limits, never approval of AI drafts. Script auto-execution remains unverified. Distinguish lightweight read-only Brain Talk callback receipts from task/schedule records; do not promise live delivery without proof.

# 2026-11-24 Short-check wording draft
Clarify that source-supported natural in-number/from-now read-only checks use
Brain Talk's saved due receipt, separate from tasks and recurring schedules.
No general timed action or due-delivery guarantee. Hold publication for the
matching rollout; retain existing task authority and person-review boundaries.
